+# Answer: `fs.rmSync` options in Node 22
+
+## The options Node 22 documents
+
+Signature: `fs.rmSync(path[, options])`. It works like the POSIX `rm` utility.
+
+| Option | Type | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `force` | boolean | `false` | When `true`, no error is thrown if `path` doesn't exist. |
+| `maxRetries` | integer | `0` | How many times to retry if an `EBUSY`, `EMFILE`, `ENFILE`, `ENOTEMPTY` or `EPERM` error happens. Retries wait `retryDelay` ms longer each time (linear backoff). Only applies when `recursive` is `true`. |
+| `recursive` | boolean | `false` | When `true`, deletes the directory and everything in it. In recursive mode, failed operations are retried. |
+| `retryDelay` | integer | `100` | Milliseconds to wait between retries. Only applies when `recursive` is `true`. Default is `100`. |
+
+## Which one fixes it: `recursive: true`
+
+```js
+fs.rmSync(dir, { recursive: true });
+// or, to also skip the error when dir doesn't exist (like `rm -rf`):
+fs.rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });
+```
+
+`force` does **not** fix this. It only stops the error when the path is missing.
+`maxRetries` and `retryDelay` only help with temporary errors such as locked files on Windows, and they only take effect together with `recursive: true`.
+
+## Checked on Node v22.23.4
+
+```
+fs.rmSync("d")                       -> ERR_FS_EISDIR "Path is a directory: rm returned EISDIR (is a directory)"
+fs.rmSync("d", {recursive:true})     -> removed, existsSync("d") === false
+fs.rmSync("nope")                    -> ENOENT
+fs.rmSync("nope", {force:true})      -> no error
+fs.rmSync(emptyDir)                  -> ERR_FS_EISDIR
+```
+
+Without `recursive`, `fs.rmSync` throws `ERR_FS_EISDIR` for **every** directory, empty ones included. The problem isn't that the folder has files in it. `rmSync` refuses to delete any directory unless you pass `recursive: true`. (To delete only an empty directory, use `fs.rmdirSync`.)
+
+Source: Node.js v22 docs, File system → `fs.rmSync(path[, options])`
+(https://nodejs.org/docs/latest-v22.x/api/fs.html#fsrmsyncpath-options).
